	(text "DESIGN NOTES\nGain law (all 7 sends): 0 V = -82.8 dB (mute, still passes signal), 2.0475 V = +10.1 dB,\n  45.4 dB/V = 0.022 dB per DAC code (MCP4728, 2.048 V internal ref, gain x1). 0 dB at 1.825 V.\nTemperature compensation: pad 42.2k || NTC 47k B4050 per scaler; drift < 0.05 dB above -40 dB, < 0.08 dB above -60 dB, 10-45 C.\n  Place each NTC against its SSI2164: TH1-TH4 at U1, TH5-TH7 at U2.\nCV filter: 2-pole MFB, -3 dB at 300 Hz, Q 0.63 (no overshoot). VC pins driven directly\n  (10k inputs; any series resistance would scale the law).\nSend 4: U2 ch3+ch4 ganged per datasheet Fig. 7 (one Rin/RC, outputs and VC tied): -3 dB noise.\nPolarity: inverting buffer + inverting VCA stage = sends in phase with AUDIO_IN.\nOutputs drive the AUX buses through 10k summing resistors (as the MIX bus): the master needs one virtual-earth amp\n  per bus (10k feedback = unity per channel). DC offsets add on the bus: AC-couple or servo the bus amps.\nMODE open = Class AB (-96 dBu noise per channel at 20k). Fit R(M) 22k for Class A."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 291 120.65 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2ff21e3a-fac3-4e2b-b2ac-a53dc3369bd8")
	)
